# r107b_caustics-visible: FEATURE follow-up to r107_caustics.fixed.py (applies ON TOP of it; branch
# when published: visual/glass-water). Context: bbfss-ctx-glass-water-caustics.md, section
# "2026-11-15 r107b diagnosis".
#
# Why r107 showed nothing (slot batch b8, sewer-water, 2026-11-15 21:45):
#  1. The sewer is roofed. r107's sun gate was the alpha of the game's screen shadow target, which
#     says "lit" under a roof the game's sun shadow does not hold (the volumetric-leak finding: roofs
#     are no sun casters; the game keeps interiors dark with light sets without sun). So the sun
#     "drew" there (47,608 px a dispatch) - a fault, not a feature. Now the sun also needs the
#     game's light set at the water point to have the sun (the r81 area gate's rule), read from the
#     directional draw's table and the G-buffer's specular target (its alpha byte); no sets in a
#     frame: no sun caustics (fail closed).
#  2. Its drawn pixels were invisible even in the test view: the cyan tint was 0.35 x w (w about
#     0.1-0.3: 3-10%) and the sun's light it moved does not exist in a sewer lit by lamps.
#  3. The walls beside the water were orange (not water) because the water test asked the depth at
#     the water point to lie ON the plane within 4 cm and the point to be seen exactly there; when
#     the depth holds the ground under the water (water not in the depth at the first blended
#     draw), both fail. Now: water = nothing in front of the point, and the surface there not
#     above the plane (on it: the water; below it: the ground under it, seen through it). The log's
#     r107b line counts on-plane against below-plane water points, which settles which it is.
#  4. NEW, the owner's goal: lamp caustics (BB_CAUSTICS_LAMPS, with or without BB_CAUSTICS): up to 4
#     lamps of the game's light grid a frame, mirrored in the plane; light ADDED where the path
#     crosses water (albedo x colour x the game's curve x facing x Schlick x pattern x 2.5).
#
# Files: r107's own (host_shaders/caustics.comp, caustics_layout.h; renderer_vulkan/caustics_params.h,
# vk_caustics.h, vk_caustics.cpp; tests/test_caustics.cpp), and three shared ones, each edit inside
# or next to r107's own lines or a hook of the same kind: vk_rasterizer_effects.cpp (r107's
# OnGBufferDraw call; the lamps before point_shadow->OnLightDraw; the light sets at the directional
# draw, after r81's AreaGate call), tests/test_effect_pipelines.cpp (r107's row), README.md (r107's
# paragraph and two rows). Nothing else; no new file.
#
# Off (BB_CAUSTICS and BB_CAUSTICS_LAMPS unset): as r107: the rasterizer makes no Caustics, each
# hook is one null pointer test; no shader build other than caustics.comp changes.
#
# Use: python -I -X utf8 r107b_caustics-visible.py check | apply | revert. Root from R107B_ROOT or
# R107_ROOT, else <tree>. Each edit is an exact text (old -> new) found exactly once;
# "applied" = every new text once and its old one gone, "clean" = every old text once and no new
# one; anything else is refused (exit 1, nothing written). Line ends are kept (CRLF in the tree).
# apply keeps the touched files in r107b_backup/ next to this script. Revert r107b BEFORE r107:
# r107's script refuses its files while r107b is on them. Exit: 0 done, 1 refused, 2 usage.
